Every clinician should explicitly and realistically discuss an expected-opioid-benefit with a patient.
Every clinician should explain a limited-long-term-opioid-pain-evidence with a patient.
Every clinician should explain a limited-long-term-opioid-function-evidence with a patient.
Every clinician should explain an unlikely-complete-pain-elimination with a patient.
There is no robust-long-term-opioid-pain-improvement-evidence.
There is no robust-long-term-opioid-function-improvement-evidence.
It is possible that an opioid-therapy does not likely eliminate a pain completely.
